The issue was that `typer.launch` in `typer/main.py` was unconditionally calling `.wait()` on the process when launching HTTP/HTTPS URLs on macOS and Linux/BSD, ignoring the `wait` parameter. I updated the implementation to check the `wait` parameter and only call `.wait()` if it is `True`, otherwise returning `0`. This behavior is now consistent with other launch paths in the library.

Verified the fix with a test script mocking `platform.system` and `subprocess.Popen`.

